request:
version 0 — the key must not exist — and a put if that holds

POST /v3/kv/txn
{
  "compare": [
    {
      "key": "Y2Fz",
      "result": "EQUAL",
      "target": "VERSION",
      "version": "0"
    }
  ],
  "failure": [
    {
      "requestRange": {
        "key": "Y2Fz"
      }
    }
  ],
  "success": [
    {
      "requestPut": {
        "key": "Y2Fz",
        "value": "bWluZQ=="
      }
    }
  ]
}

response:
succeeded true, and the put's own response inside `responses`

HTTP 200 OK
{
  "header": {
    "cluster_id": "16534609535171932234",
    "member_id": "715399635594886098",
    "raft_term": "2",
    "revision": "2"
  },
  "responses": [
    {
      "response_put": {
        "header": {
          "revision": "2"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "succeeded": true
}

